Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Noong Enero po, na-hit po kami ng earthquake swarms.

asr-000706
00:34:45.280 --> 00:34:47.440
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Ilang preemptive evacuation po

asr-000707
00:34:47.440 --> 00:34:49.240
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: ang kinailangan naming gawin.

asr-000708
00:34:49.879 --> 00:34:57.900
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Sobrang nakatulong po sila Director Bacolcol at mga kaibigan natin sa PHIVOLCS,

asr-000709
00:34:59.640 --> 00:35:02.760
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: hindi lang sa pag-monitor ng tsunami warnings,

asr-000710
00:35:02.760 --> 00:35:07.160
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: but even bumaba po sila para sa hazard mapping,

asr-000711
00:35:07.160 --> 00:35:12.460
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: sa REDAS seminar sa buong coastal namin sa Kalamansig, Lebak, at Palimbang.

asr-000712
00:35:13.160 --> 00:35:16.280
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Maraming-maraming salamat po kay Director Toto

asr-000713
00:35:16.280 --> 00:35:18.580
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: at sa lahat po ng kaibigan natin sa PHIVOLCS,

asr-000714
00:35:18.880 --> 00:35:20.960
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: at kay Dr. Servando po,

asr-000715
00:35:20.960 --> 00:35:23.000
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: na grabe po 'yung pagkulit ko sa kanya

asr-000716
00:35:23.000 --> 00:35:26.880
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: noong nag-start po 'yung advisory sa El Niño,

asr-000717
00:35:26.880 --> 00:35:29.800
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: kasi ang Sultan Kudarat po ay isa sa mga pinaka-vulnerable

asr-000718
00:35:30.079 --> 00:35:32.320
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: sa super El Niño pagdating.

asr-000719
00:35:32.320 --> 00:35:33.839
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So maraming-maraming salamat po

asr-000720
00:35:33.839 --> 00:35:36.079
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: sa DOST family sa lahat po ng tulong ninyo,

asr-000721
00:35:36.079 --> 00:35:37.180
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: and rest assured po,

asr-000722
00:35:37.800 --> 00:35:40.160
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: suportado po natin hindi lang po 'yung budget ninyo,

asr-000723
00:35:40.160 --> 00:35:41.679
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: pero pati 'yung pagdagdag

asr-000724
00:35:42.880 --> 00:35:44.600
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: ng budget ninyo sa DOST.

asr-000725
00:35:45.119 --> 00:35:45.900
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Maraming-maraming salamat po.

asr-000726
00:35:48.760 --> 00:35:50.020
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Thank you, Kong Bella.

asr-000727
00:35:50.960 --> 00:35:52.860
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Now, from the minority,

asr-000728
00:35:55.599 --> 00:35:57.480
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Congressman Antonio Tinio.

asr-000729
00:36:02.560 --> 00:36:03.260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Thank you chair.

asr-000730
00:36:03.800 --> 00:36:06.840
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ah ilang mga paglilinaw sa proposed budget

asr-000731
00:36:09.839 --> 00:36:14.860
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: so total budget uh proposed 30.8

asr-000732
00:36:15.040 --> 00:36:21.520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: no, na mas mababa kaysa GAA ngayon na 32.1 billion.

asr-000733
00:36:21.520 --> 00:36:23.280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So nabawasan. Tapos

asr-000734
00:36:23.280 --> 00:36:28.520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: kung tinitignan natin yung budget ng DOST and attached

asr-000735
00:36:28.520 --> 00:36:31.799
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: of course there's a reduction in the sa Office of the Secretary.

asr-000736
00:36:32.480 --> 00:36:39.160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tapos sa mga attached agencies merong mga you know ah malaki rin.

asr-000737
00:36:39.160 --> 00:36:47.160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: For example, PAGASA, nabawasan po by 2 point...

asr-000738
00:36:47.160 --> 00:36:49.020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Magkano itong nabawas dito?

asr-000739
00:36:49.800 --> 00:36:52.839
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: It's a 12.5%

asr-000740
00:36:52.839 --> 00:36:53.280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tama po ba?

asr-000741
00:36:53.280 --> 00:36:54.880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ah, so PAGASA,

asr-000742
00:36:54.880 --> 00:36:59.760
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ano pong explanation? Bakit

asr-000743
00:36:59.760 --> 00:37:04.319
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: mas mababa po ang ang proposal ng PAGASA? Um,

asr-000744
00:37:04.319 --> 00:37:05.980
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: Dr. Servando, can you respond?

asr-000745
00:37:07.680 --> 00:37:09.600
PAGASA Administrator Nathaniel T. Servando: Thank you, Secretary.

asr-000746
00:37:10.000 --> 00:37:17.579
PAGASA Administrator Nathaniel T. Servando: Your Honor, the reduction of our budget for 2027

asr-000747
00:37:18.480 --> 00:37:21.720
PAGASA Administrator Nathaniel T. Servando: on the uh capital outlay because some projects

asr-000748
00:37:22.800 --> 00:37:24.280
PAGASA Administrator Nathaniel T. Servando: for the 2026

asr-000749
00:37:24.880 --> 00:37:27.880
PAGASA Administrator Nathaniel T. Servando: ay hindi na kailangang mapunduhan na next year

asr-000750
00:37:27.880 --> 00:37:32.079
PAGASA Administrator Nathaniel T. Servando: like example sa pag-establish ng warning system

asr-000751
00:37:32.079 --> 00:37:33.539
PAGASA Administrator Nathaniel T. Servando: sa isang river basin

asr-000752
00:37:34.000 --> 00:37:35.760
PAGASA Administrator Nathaniel T. Servando: so dahil funded na this year

asr-000753
00:37:36.760 --> 00:37:40.139
PAGASA Administrator Nathaniel T. Servando: so tinanggal na siya for next year.

asr-000754
00:37:40.160 --> 00:37:47.760
PAGASA Administrator Nathaniel T. Servando: One [unclear] equipment, like an X-band radar,

asr-000755
00:37:47.760 --> 00:37:49.840
PAGASA Administrator Nathaniel T. Servando: to be established in one of the river basin

asr-000756
00:37:50.400 --> 00:37:52.680
PAGASA Administrator Nathaniel T. Servando: ay hindi naman kailangang punduhan again

asr-000757
00:37:52.680 --> 00:37:56.280
PAGASA Administrator Nathaniel T. Servando: so uh the reduction is about on the capital outlay

asr-000758
00:37:56.280 --> 00:38:00.239
PAGASA Administrator Nathaniel T. Servando: that uh we're already excluded for next year.

asr-000759
00:38:01.280 --> 00:38:01.560
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

asr-000760
00:38:01.560 --> 00:38:06.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So hindi naman nabawasan iyung ah operations or anything.

asr-000761
00:38:07.160 --> 00:38:07.720
PAGASA Administrator Nathaniel T. Servando: Hindi naman po.

asr-000762
00:38:07.720 --> 00:38:08.920
PAGASA Administrator Nathaniel T. Servando: In fact, may increase po.

asr-000763
00:38:08.920 --> 00:38:10.260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sige. Capital outlay.

asr-000764
00:38:10.920 --> 00:38:19.080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ah ang isa pa pong tampok dito ay yung bawas sa Food and Nutrition Research Institute

asr-000765
00:38:20.079 --> 00:38:25.079
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: from uh 1.1 billion naging 634 million

asr-000766
00:38:25.079 --> 00:38:26.899
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: na lang. Ano pong explanation non?

asr-000767
00:38:28.560 --> 00:38:30.420
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: May I ask the director?

asr-000768
00:38:30.839 --> 00:38:34.760
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: I would surmise it's the building that they need to finish

asr-000769
00:38:34.760 --> 00:38:36.400
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: but please respond.

asr-000770
00:38:37.560 --> 00:38:38.960
DOST-FNRI Director Jacus S. Nacis: Salamat po secretary. Ah

asr-000771
00:38:39.400 --> 00:38:43.640
DOST-FNRI Director Jacus S. Nacis: sir um yung bawas po doon sa budget is the capital

asr-000772
00:38:43.640 --> 00:38:44.960
DOST-FNRI Director Jacus S. Nacis: capital outlay, gaya po ng sinabi ng Secretary.

asr-000773
00:38:44.960 --> 00:38:47.180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, pinondohan iyong building ninyo. Ganoon ba?

asr-000774
00:38:47.920 --> 00:38:48.960
DOST-FNRI Director Jacus S. Nacis: Hindi po,

asr-000775
00:38:48.960 --> 00:38:50.960
DOST-FNRI Director Jacus S. Nacis: naibawas po iyong pondo sa building.

asr-000776
00:38:50.960 --> 00:38:52.060
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kulang pa?

asr-000777
00:38:53.240 --> 00:38:55.720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ulit, nabawas?

asr-000778
00:38:55.720 --> 00:38:56.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pakilinaw.

asr-000779
00:38:57.359 --> 00:38:59.300
DOST-FNRI Director Jacus S. Nacis: Yun po yung nabawas doon sa budget po.

asr-000780
00:38:59.960 --> 00:39:04.220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So there was funding for capital outlay for 2026.

asr-000781
00:39:04.720 --> 00:39:05.280
DOST-FNRI Director Jacus S. Nacis: Yes po.

asr-000782
00:39:05.280 --> 00:39:07.020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero wala na for 2027.

asr-000783
00:39:07.160 --> 00:39:07.599
DOST-FNRI Director Jacus S. Nacis: Yes po.

asr-000784
00:39:07.599 --> 00:39:09.280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Makukumpleto na ba iyong building?

asr-000785
00:39:09.280 --> 00:39:11.280
DOST-FNRI Director Jacus S. Nacis: Phase 4 po. Hindi pa po siya makukumpleto.

asr-000786
00:39:11.280 --> 00:39:11.800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, kulang?

asr-000787
00:39:11.800 --> 00:39:12.160
DOST-FNRI Director Jacus S. Nacis: Wala.

asr-000788
00:39:12.160 --> 00:39:17.040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, kailangan ninyo ba, para matapos ang inyong building,

asr-000789
00:39:17.040 --> 00:39:17.920
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: how much do you need?

asr-000790
00:39:19.040 --> 00:39:23.160
DOST-FNRI Director Jacus S. Nacis: iyung request po for 2027 is 400 million po for the phase 4.

asr-000791
00:39:23.160 --> 00:39:25.040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 400 million for phase 4. Ayan.

asr-000792
00:39:25.040 --> 00:39:29.119
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So baka narinig yan ng ating chair of the committee on appropriations.

asr-000793
00:39:29.119 --> 00:39:29.839
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

asr-000794
00:39:29.839 --> 00:39:33.079
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sa kabilang banda naman merong merong napansin ako

asr-000795
00:39:33.079 --> 00:39:36.420
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: rito Metals Industry Research and Development Center.

asr-000796
00:39:37.560 --> 00:39:45.560
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: It's a a 73.6% increase from 316 naging 549 million.

asr-000797
00:39:45.560 --> 00:39:47.280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Bakit naman po may malaking increase?

asr-000798
00:39:47.280 --> 00:39:48.440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Capital outlay din ba to?

asr-000799
00:39:48.440 --> 00:39:49.580
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: Ako na lang sasagot.

asr-000800
00:39:49.839 --> 00:39:50.399
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Opo. Sige po.

asr-000801
00:39:51.000 --> 00:39:53.940
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: 'Yung uh grant-in-aid kasi ng Office of the Secretary,

asr-000802
00:39:54.240 --> 00:39:57.380
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: tinanggalan kami and then nilipat sa ibang mga agencies

asr-000803
00:39:57.640 --> 00:39:59.079
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: tulad ng MIRDC

asr-000804
00:39:59.079 --> 00:39:59.920
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: kaya lumaki sila.

asr-000805
00:40:01.160 --> 00:40:02.060
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Mayroon pong grant

asr-000806
00:40:02.960 --> 00:40:04.740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: sa Office of the Secretary. Nilipat ninyo doon?

asr-000807
00:40:05.079 --> 00:40:05.899
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: Oo.

asr-000808
00:40:06.079 --> 00:40:09.300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: What is the specific grant? Mukhang substansyal.

asr-000810
00:40:09.680 --> 00:40:11.940
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: Usually, some of it is related to their mandate.

asr-000811
00:40:12.520 --> 00:40:15.160
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: Usually ang ginagawa po natin sa grant-in-aid

asr-000812
00:40:15.160 --> 00:40:18.800
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: if agencies would need support from the office of the secretary

asr-000813
00:40:18.800 --> 00:40:20.700
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: to develop new technologies,

asr-000814
00:40:21.160 --> 00:40:24.600
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: especially po iyung tinatawag naming industry 4.0

asr-000815
00:40:25.720 --> 00:40:27.940
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: using AI robotics automation,

asr-000816
00:40:29.000 --> 00:40:31.220
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: ito po yung tinatawag naming Quatro program.

asr-000817
00:40:31.640 --> 00:40:36.180
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: Binibigyan namin sila ng fund because it's not part of their original GIA fund.

asr-000818
00:40:36.760 --> 00:40:43.140
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: So nag-decide ang DBM to transfer uh that certain amount of fund to them.

asr-000819
00:40:44.520 --> 00:40:48.160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So pag sinabi pong Metals Industry Research and Development Center,

asr-000820
00:40:48.160 --> 00:40:50.659
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: specifically, you're talking about robotics ba iyong binanggit ninyo?

asr-000821
00:40:51.359 --> 00:40:53.440
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: Well, it's about metals industry but

asr-000822
00:40:54.400 --> 00:40:55.260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Is that mining? Ganoon ba?

asr-000823
00:40:56.079 --> 00:40:57.139
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: Not really.

asr-000824
00:40:57.640 --> 00:40:58.899
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: advanced manufacturing

asr-000826
00:40:59.359 --> 00:41:03.180
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: That would include metal and other advanced manufacturing technologies,

asr-000827
00:41:03.640 --> 00:41:06.720
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: including robotics automation mechanization.

asr-000828
00:41:07.280 --> 00:41:07.520
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: Okay?

asr-000829
00:41:08.240 --> 00:41:09.319
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sige po.

asr-000830
00:41:09.319 --> 00:41:11.680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ah, kasama sa presentation ninyo,

asr-000831
00:41:11.680 --> 00:41:19.160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: may banggit dito tungkol sa NAICRI, National AI Center for Research and Innovation.

asr-000832
00:41:19.160 --> 00:41:20.880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Although in your budget proposal

asr-000833
00:41:20.880 --> 00:41:24.160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: parang wala namang specific as far as I know

asr-000834
00:41:24.160 --> 00:41:25.460
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: item for the center.

asr-000835
00:41:26.560 --> 00:41:28.440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tama po ba?

asr-000836
00:41:28.440 --> 00:41:33.839
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: this is already being funded at the uh grant in aid level

asr-000837
00:41:33.839 --> 00:41:36.260
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: as this is a continuing R&amp;D program

asr-000838
00:41:36.800 --> 00:41:40.000
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: but the Advanced Science and Technology Institute

asr-000839
00:41:40.000 --> 00:41:43.920
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: also has a proposal to further increase the compute power.

asr-000840
00:41:43.920 --> 00:41:48.280
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: So I'll ask the Director of ASTI, Dr. de Leon, to further explain.

asr-000841
00:41:48.280 --> 00:41:50.119
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yeah. And in connection with that,

asr-000842
00:41:50.119 --> 00:41:57.200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: so uh sa press release sa inyong website regarding the National AI strategy for the Philippines,

asr-000843
00:41:58.040 --> 00:42:03.540
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: the Secretary mentioned high-performance compute,

asr-000844
00:42:05.280 --> 00:42:07.320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: national high-performance compute centers,

asr-000845
00:42:09.000 --> 00:42:17.720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: and that you have a target of increasing high-performance computing power by 26-fold,

asr-000846
00:42:17.720 --> 00:42:19.500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: presumably, of government?

asr-000847
00:42:20.359 --> 00:42:22.559
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: Yes. For for our own operation

asr-000848
00:42:22.559 --> 00:42:23.320
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: of government

asr-000849
00:42:23.640 --> 00:42:29.579
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: and application especially to support our MSME and industries to use AI.

asr-000850
00:42:30.200 --> 00:42:30.760
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sige. Puwede

asr-000851
00:42:30.760 --> 00:42:32.960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: po bang paki-elaborate

asr-000852
00:42:32.960 --> 00:42:36.580
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ano po itong high-performance computing?

asr-000853
00:42:37.520 --> 00:42:37.820
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sorry.

asr-000854
00:42:38.480 --> 00:42:39.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ano ba? High-power...

asr-000855
00:42:40.000 --> 00:42:41.240
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: High-performance computing.

asr-000856
00:42:41.240 --> 00:42:44.580
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. High-power computing center.

asr-000858
00:42:44.720 --> 00:42:46.000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: What is this exactly?

asr-000859
00:42:46.480 --> 00:42:46.920
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: Okay.

asr-000860
00:42:46.920 --> 00:42:47.599
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: So I'll ask...

asr-000861
00:42:47.599 --> 00:42:53.019
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Is this infrastructure, as in data centers?

asr-000862
00:42:53.520 --> 00:42:55.119
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: Essentially it's a compute center.

asr-000863
00:42:55.119 --> 00:42:56.200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Compute center.

asr-000864
00:42:56.200 --> 00:42:56.720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Compute

asr-000865
00:42:56.720 --> 00:42:57.440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: cluster?

asr-000866
00:42:57.440 --> 00:42:58.240
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: AI ba iyan?

asr-000867
00:42:58.240 --> 00:42:58.800
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: Yeah. AI.

asr-000868
00:42:58.800 --> 00:43:01.880
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: It can be both physical and on cloud.

asr-000869
00:43:01.880 --> 00:43:03.620
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So you're talking about...

asr-000870
00:43:04.960 --> 00:43:05.200
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: Yes.

asr-000871
00:43:05.200 --> 00:43:06.040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, in-country?

asr-000872
00:43:06.040 --> 00:43:06.640
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: In-country po iyan.

asr-000874
00:43:06.640 --> 00:43:08.200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So that we can have our own.

asr-000875
00:43:08.200 --> 00:43:08.720
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: Yes.

asr-000876
00:43:08.720 --> 00:43:12.839
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, mga high-power GPUs for AI.

asr-000877
00:43:12.839 --> 00:43:13.119
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: Yes.

asr-000879
00:43:13.119 --> 00:43:15.280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Opo. Puwede po bang mabigyan tayo ng detalye

asr-000882
00:43:15.280 --> 00:43:17.480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: noong anong mga processor ito?

asr-000883
00:43:17.480 --> 00:43:18.400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Gaano karami?

asr-000884
00:43:18.760 --> 00:43:19.920
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: How big is the cluster?

asr-000885
00:43:20.280 --> 00:43:21.539
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Where do you get your power?

asr-000886
00:43:22.119 --> 00:43:26.559
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Iyan iyong kontrobersiya kaugnay sa Pax Silica.

asr-000887
00:43:26.559 --> 00:43:33.220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And also, I would like to know ano ba ang level ng AI infrastructure na nasa Pilipinas

asr-000888
00:43:33.680 --> 00:43:38.040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: at pag-aari ng gobyerno in this case?

asr-000889
00:43:38.480 --> 00:43:48.579
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: I am aware may mga private companies na nagtatayo sila ng sarili nilang AI on-prem data centers

asr-000890
00:43:49.920 --> 00:43:50.600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: for AI.

asr-000891
00:43:51.680 --> 00:43:56.480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Paano dito sa Pilipinas? Paano iyong Pilipinas?

asr-000892
00:43:56.480 --> 00:43:58.040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So pwede po bang mag-explain?

asr-000893
00:43:58.040 --> 00:43:58.880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yeah please.

asr-000894
00:43:58.880 --> 00:43:59.560
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Director Franz.

asr-000895
00:44:00.160 --> 00:44:02.060
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At magkano iyong budget nito?

asr-000907
00:44:03.319 --> 00:44:06.260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And is this reflected in the budget proposal?

asr-000908
00:44:08.920 --> 00:44:12.720
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: Thank you, Secretary, Madam Chair, Your Honor.

asr-000909
00:44:13.480 --> 00:44:19.000
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: Iyong NAICRI po is a continuation of the current service being provided by the Advanced Science

asr-000910
00:44:19.000 --> 00:44:19.999
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: and Technology Institute.

asr-000911
00:44:20.839 --> 00:44:28.720
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: So, mga one decade ago, nagtayo na po ng high-performance supercomputer cluster po na mina-manage po ng ASTI

asr-000912
00:44:28.720 --> 00:44:32.359
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: ASTI and then it became a shared service.

asr-000913
00:44:32.359 --> 00:44:42.740
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: So ibig sabihin po, binibigay natin iyong compute resources and storage for other government agencies, R&amp;D institutes, and the academic community.

asr-000914
00:44:43.079 --> 00:44:50.960
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: Of course, with the advent of AI, it needed a different type of architecture, different type of AI hardware.

asr-000915
00:44:50.960 --> 00:44:53.659
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: So ito na po iyong mga GPU-based computers po natin.

asr-000916
00:44:54.160 --> 00:44:57.280
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: So through the years, through the different projects,

asr-000917
00:44:57.280 --> 00:45:01.680
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: nabibigyan po tayo ng pondo to expand that center.

asr-000918
00:45:02.359 --> 00:45:12.200
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: With NAICRI, it's more of institutionalizing and sustaining the AI track being supported by DOST.

asr-000919
00:45:12.599 --> 00:45:15.960
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: So nandun po yung commitment to expand further

asr-000920
00:45:15.960 --> 00:45:18.960
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: as you mentioned po yung nabasa po ninyo sa press release

asr-000921
00:45:19.359 --> 00:45:21.100
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: and panimula pa lang po siya.

asr-000922
00:45:22.119 --> 00:45:26.079
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: If we could imagine for example currently meron po kaming maliit na data center

asr-000923
00:45:26.079 --> 00:45:29.040
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: is just a container van at the back of our office.

asr-000924
00:45:29.040 --> 00:45:31.080
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: Ganun lang po kaliit doon po nagsisimula.

asr-000925
00:45:31.760 --> 00:45:36.120
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: Ngayon po we are starting to expand through commercial data centers.

asr-000926
00:45:37.640 --> 00:45:42.659
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: rent out po tayo ng space and then we install our own um GPUs.

asr-000927
00:45:42.680 --> 00:45:47.360
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: So ang intent po natin um to further enhance our own sovereignty.

asr-000928
00:45:47.720 --> 00:45:54.839
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: Yung pagkakaroon po natin ng capacity to deploy and um make our own AI based application

asr-000929
00:45:54.839 --> 00:45:56.520
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: using our own

asr-000930
00:45:56.520 --> 00:46:00.020
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: system. Iyon po iyong sinusuportahan ng DOST sa ngayon.

asr-000931
00:46:01.880 --> 00:46:03.680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Hindi po ma-provide ng...

asr-000932
00:46:03.680 --> 00:46:14.899
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Magkaroon ng idea, ang kongreso, ano yung level ng technology na meron ng DOST ngayon.

asr-000933
00:46:15.119 --> 00:46:17.600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: For example, sabi nyo may isang container van kayo.

asr-000934
00:46:18.280 --> 00:46:21.459
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At sa ngayon, yan ang inyong high power compute.

asr-000935
00:46:22.160 --> 00:46:24.079
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So ano yung mga processor nyo?

asr-000936
00:46:24.079 --> 00:46:24.439
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Is this...

asr-000937
00:46:25.800 --> 00:46:26.520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Latest ba ito?

asr-000938
00:46:26.520 --> 00:46:28.480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Di ba mga NVIDIA chips?

asr-000939
00:46:28.480 --> 00:46:32.880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: A100, H100, Blackwell, iyong mga ganoon.

asr-000940
00:46:32.880 --> 00:46:33.439
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Nasaan tayo?

asr-000941
00:46:34.240 --> 00:46:35.480
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: So tama pa yung nabanggitin nyo.

asr-000942
00:46:35.480 --> 00:46:36.520
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: Meron po tayo noon.

asr-000943
00:46:37.040 --> 00:46:40.480
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: With the latest iteration po na expansion po natin,

asr-000944
00:46:40.480 --> 00:46:45.820
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: we were fortunate enough to procure yung mas bago, H200.

asr-000945
00:46:45.920 --> 00:46:48.640
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: So currently, in-install po natin sila.

asr-000946
00:46:49.079 --> 00:46:51.359
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: And then with the establishment of NAICRI,

asr-000947
00:46:51.359 --> 00:46:53.640
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: it's not just about the expansion of the current,

asr-000948
00:46:53.640 --> 00:46:54.800
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: but we also took...

asr-000949
00:46:54.800 --> 00:46:57.079
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: plan to roll out sa regions.

asr-000950
00:46:57.079 --> 00:47:03.839
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: Because we realized, masyadong nakasentro yung compute power sa NCR o sa Mega Manila.

asr-000951
00:47:03.839 --> 00:47:06.940
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: So we want to expand that resource as well to the regions.

asr-000952
00:47:07.640 --> 00:47:12.800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So nabanggit nyo po, H200, ilan po yung cluster nyo, ilang processors po yun?

asr-000953
00:47:12.800 --> 00:47:20.500
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: Opo, I don't have the exact figure, but I think there are five major compute servers.

asr-000954
00:47:20.520 --> 00:47:25.200
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: Bukod po sa compute servers, may tandem po siya with data storage,

asr-000955
00:47:25.200 --> 00:47:26.599
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: kasi mahalaga rin po siya.

asr-000956
00:47:26.599 --> 00:47:29.599
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: And also upgrading of network equipment.

asr-000957
00:47:29.599 --> 00:47:34.359
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: Kasi we expect large amount of data and traffic to be exchanged.

asr-000958
00:47:34.359 --> 00:47:36.820
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: So lahat po yun, sabay-sabay po natin na in-upgrade.

asr-000959
00:47:37.359 --> 00:47:38.520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At magkano po ang budget?

asr-000960
00:47:38.520 --> 00:47:40.160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Is that in the current budget?

asr-000961
00:47:40.160 --> 00:47:46.119
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And the proposal to expand by 26-fold by 2028?

asr-000962
00:47:46.119 --> 00:47:47.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So magkano po yung...

asr-000963
00:47:48.839 --> 00:47:49.940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: How much will this cost?

asr-000964
00:47:50.520 --> 00:47:55.000
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: Opo, sa ngayon po iyong initial seed funding na binigay po ng DOST

asr-000965
00:47:55.000 --> 00:47:57.240
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: through its GIAs, 300 million.

asr-000966
00:47:57.800 --> 00:47:59.740
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: So we hope to further that.

asr-000967
00:47:59.760 --> 00:48:04.640
DOST-ASTI Director Franz A. de Leon: So aside from the OSEC, probably in the near future, also through developmental partners po.

asr-000968
00:48:05.520 --> 00:48:06.040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

asr-000969
00:48:06.040 --> 00:48:10.720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So Chair, hindi na ako magpapatagal, pero masang concern po natin dito.

asr-000970
00:48:10.720 --> 00:48:23.220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yun nga, importante yung binabanggit na dapat magkaroon din ng sariling digital or AI infrastructure ang Pilipinas.

asr-000971
00:48:24.000 --> 00:48:24.300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No?

asr-000972
00:48:24.960 --> 00:48:29.020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So yung tinatawag na, whatever you call it, data sovereignty.

asr-000973
00:48:29.640 --> 00:48:29.880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

asr-000974
00:48:30.800 --> 00:48:44.720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Otherwise, ang nangyayari po, lumalaga na pang AI, palagi tayong uupa ng cloud and data services and AI services from, ultimately from abroad.

asr-000975
00:48:45.480 --> 00:48:45.720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Diba?

asr-000976
00:48:45.720 --> 00:48:47.200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At papalaki na ng papalaki.

asr-000977
00:48:47.200 --> 00:48:49.240
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Actually, ang ginagastos natin dyan.

asr-000978
00:48:49.240 --> 00:48:55.559
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, Chair, pwedeng makahingi na lang makapagsubmit ng mas na detalyado.

asr-000979
00:48:55.559 --> 00:49:06.040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung information about what we currently have and what are the plans to expand the nationally owned compute.

asr-000980
00:49:06.920 --> 00:49:07.240
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No?

asr-000981
00:49:08.079 --> 00:49:12.840
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And also the plan to, sabi nyo, dapat ma-expand din sa regions.

asr-000982
00:49:13.400 --> 00:49:13.640
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Diba?

asr-000983
00:49:14.359 --> 00:49:14.659
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

asr-000984
00:49:15.280 --> 00:49:21.880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, tapos, in other words, kasi minsan pagkausap namin ng DICT, parang pinag-uusapan din nila ito.

asr-000985
00:49:21.880 --> 00:49:22.400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, ano ba yan?

asr-000986
00:49:23.880 --> 00:49:45.240
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And kayo ba ang lead agency with regard to, you know, developing indigenous digital infrastructure o yung AI infrastructure o is it DICT o may kanya-kanyang diskarte kayo?

asr-000987
00:49:46.680 --> 00:49:48.160
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: Mr. Chair, if I may respond.

asr-000988
00:49:48.880 --> 00:49:51.040
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: We developed the National AI Strategy.

asr-000989
00:49:51.559 --> 00:49:55.440
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: And in that development, there are four major components.

asr-000990
00:49:55.440 --> 00:50:05.580
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: The first is the AI factory, the infrastructure, the human resources, the policies, and of course the financing.

asr-000991
00:50:06.079 --> 00:50:18.300
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: Out of it, we will have to develop the AI refinery, developing the models, the analytics between government, national, local, academic, and industry partners.

asr-000992
00:50:18.599 --> 00:50:20.799
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: Now, to really implement and accelerate.

asr-000993
00:50:20.799 --> 00:50:29.160
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: The application of AI, we need to have partnerships at the local, regional, and national level, and of course, international partnership.

asr-000994
00:50:29.799 --> 00:50:35.900
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: All of this are geared into really helping our own enterprises and the community.

asr-000995
00:50:36.480 --> 00:50:45.559
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: So, we also crafted the National AI Implementation Strategy, where different government organizations will take the lead.

asr-000996
00:50:45.559 --> 00:50:51.360
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: On DOST, we lead in the development of the infrastructure for research and development.

asr-000997
00:50:51.680 --> 00:51:02.220
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: And talent management, and development of language models that can be utilized together with DTI and DICT, and the industry by various enterprises.

asr-000998
00:51:02.839 --> 00:51:12.119
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: Now, DICT is involved in the connectivity and infrastructure as well, but they are mainly dealing with the private sector to support this.

asr-000999
00:51:12.119 --> 00:51:14.340
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: Magkaiba po talaga ang laro namin.

asr-001000
00:51:14.839 --> 00:51:21.040
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: Now, to support the AI sovereignty, DOST is also developing.

asr-001001
00:51:21.319 --> 00:51:26.800
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: The data sovereignty through the Geospatial Analytics and Technology Solutions platform.

asr-001002
00:51:27.359 --> 00:51:33.920
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: It's a digital transformation of all data anchored on geographic information system, the science of where.

asr-001003
00:51:34.559 --> 00:51:39.760
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: And this is where we differentiate DOST from the rest of other government agencies.

asr-001004
00:51:39.760 --> 00:51:46.640
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: We are developing this data that will be utilized to fuel the artificial intelligence technology.

asr-001005
00:51:47.119 --> 00:51:50.400
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: So, eventually, our goal is to develop a geospatial.

asr-001006
00:51:50.400 --> 00:52:08.880
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: GeoAI Hub, managed by DOST, so that we can provide our enterprises and the government Philippine-owned data that will be queried by large language models or language models that we develop.

asr-001007
00:52:08.880 --> 00:52:17.680
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: Currently, we have iTanong as a language model that can be utilized by anyone who would want to look at it.

asr-001008
00:52:17.680 --> 00:52:20.559
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: We also have an equivalent of the App Store or Google.

asr-001009
00:52:20.559 --> 00:52:30.960
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: We also have a Google Play Store where language models using Filipino data sets are placed there so that one can look at it and see if you have similar operation.

asr-001010
00:52:30.960 --> 00:52:36.720
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: You can use that model para i-short circuit na po natin yung lack of compute power and scale.

asr-001011
00:52:36.720 --> 00:52:41.799
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: So, gamitin nyo na lang yun, pwede mo nang patakbuhin yung operation mo using that model.

asr-001012
00:52:41.799 --> 00:52:45.440
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: So iyon po ang current state ng AI strategy ng DOST.

asr-001013
00:52:46.359 --> 00:52:50.860
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sir, pahingin na lang po, sana makapag-provide ng mga data.

asr-001014
00:52:51.400 --> 00:52:55.900
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Mga dokumento on the national AI strategy and the plan.

asr-001015
00:52:57.599 --> 00:53:06.520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And yung ibang mga tanong ko, siguro, sino po ba ang magandang kausap si Director De Leon?

asr-001016
00:53:06.520 --> 00:53:06.820
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: Opo.

asr-001017
00:53:07.359 --> 00:53:08.660
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay, thank you. Thank you, Chair.

asr-001018
00:53:09.960 --> 00:53:11.220
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Thank you, Congressman Tinio.

asr-001019
00:53:13.240 --> 00:53:15.008
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Congressman Nicky Briones.

asr-001020
00:53:16.839 --> 00:53:19.000
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Ah, thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-001021
00:53:19.000 --> 00:53:21.960
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Ah, gusto ko lang namang magpasalamat

asr-001022
00:53:21.960 --> 00:53:27.799
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: sa mga nagagawa na itutulong ng DOST sa ating mga farmers,

asr-001023
00:53:27.799 --> 00:53:32.359
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: especially sa amin, sa egg industry.

asr-001024
00:53:32.359 --> 00:53:41.119
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: through your program na DOST-BIST, or Business Innovation through Science and Technology,

asr-001025
00:53:41.119 --> 00:53:48.400
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: CRADLE, uh, Collaborative Research and Development to Leverage Philippine Economy,

asr-001026
00:53:48.400 --> 00:53:51.480
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: malaki ang naitulong ng DOST.

asr-001027
00:53:51.480 --> 00:54:01.200
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Without my intervention, ha, kaya yung coordination ng DOST at saka ng DA, napakaganda.

asr-001028
00:54:01.200 --> 00:54:07.920
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Kasi alam natin na yung egg eh maiksi lang ang shelf life.

asr-001029
00:54:07.920 --> 00:54:14.040
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: So dahil doon sa inyong boiled egg brine solution,

asr-001030
00:54:14.040 --> 00:54:17.520
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: pwede tumagal yung boiled egg up to five years.

asr-001031
00:54:17.520 --> 00:54:21.200
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: So yung handling sa, let's say, may calamity,

asr-001032
00:54:21.200 --> 00:54:25.480
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: or gusto nating tulungan yung nutrition ng ating mga bata,

asr-001033
00:54:25.480 --> 00:54:29.640
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: madali na iparating.

asr-001034
00:54:29.640 --> 00:54:39.280
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: So ang isa pa, yung, ah, sa aming, ah, itong, ah, egg processing plant.

asr-001035
00:54:39.280 --> 00:54:43.040
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Una, yung liquefied egg processing plant.

asr-001036
00:54:43.040 --> 00:54:48.480
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Ang ating itlog, up to 10, 12 days, pwede nang masira.

asr-001037
00:54:48.480 --> 00:54:51.079
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Pero because of this liquefied

asr-001038
00:54:51.079 --> 00:54:56.200
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: egg processing plant, through your initiative,

asr-001039
00:54:56.200 --> 00:55:03.160
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: ah, nagla-last ng up to more than a month, more than five months.

asr-001040
00:55:03.160 --> 00:55:15.079
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: So mas mabilis yung pagde-deliver din sa mga hotel and industrial partner namin.

asr-001041
00:55:15.079 --> 00:55:17.559
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Kaya malaki ang nagagawa.

asr-001042
00:55:17.559 --> 00:55:21.440
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: At lastly, itong egg powder,

asr-001043
00:55:21.440 --> 00:55:22.280
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Egg.

asr-001044
00:55:22.280 --> 00:55:24.640
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Powder processing plant.

asr-001045
00:55:24.640 --> 00:55:29.240
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: na even up to five years,

asr-001046
00:55:29.240 --> 00:55:31.440
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: ah, tumatagal yung itlog.

asr-001047
00:55:31.440 --> 00:55:39.520
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: So, napakalaki ng, uh, nagawa niyo sa Batangas Egg Producers Cooperative

asr-001048
00:55:39.520 --> 00:55:41.920
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: at doon sa aming bayan sa San Jose,

asr-001049
00:55:41.920 --> 00:55:44.280
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: which is the egg basket of the Philippines.

asr-001050
00:55:44.280 --> 00:55:48.079
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: We are producing 12 million eggs a day.

asr-001051
00:55:48.079 --> 00:55:51.039
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: So, thank you, ah,

asr-001052
00:55:51.039 --> 00:55:51.839
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: DOST

asr-001053
00:55:51.839 --> 00:55:52.599
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Secretary

asr-001054
00:55:52.599 --> 00:55:53.760
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Renato Solidum.

asr-001055
00:55:53.760 --> 00:55:59.559
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Sana talagang madagdagan natin ang budget ng DOST.

asr-001056
00:55:59.559 --> 00:56:00.599
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Thank you po.

asr-001057
00:56:00.599 --> 00:56:01.075
Rep. Nicanor M. Briones: Thank you.

asr-001058
00:56:01.440 --> 00:56:04.349
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Thank you, Vice Chair Nicky Briones.

asr-001059
00:56:04.535 --> 00:56:09.319
Rep. Amben S. Amante: First, I would like to acknowledge the presence of our Senior Deputy Speaker,

asr-001060
00:56:09.319 --> 00:56:11.880
Rep. Amben S. Amante: the gentleman, Senior Deputy Speaker

asr-001061
00:56:11.880 --> 00:56:13.124
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Dan Fernandez.

asr-001062
00:56:13.310 --> 00:56:14.255
Rep. Dan S. Fernandez: Baka ako ang makakadagdag ng budget?

asr-001063
00:56:16.972 --> 00:56:19.870
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Before we go to our favorite motion,

asr-001064
00:56:20.680 --> 00:56:22.440
Rep. Amben S. Amante: any last word of support?

asr-001065
00:56:22.440 --> 00:56:25.173
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Senior Deputy Speaker.

asr-001066
00:56:30.303 --> 00:56:34.000
Rep. Dan S. Fernandez: Humabol lang ako, but I'm not going to ask questions.

asr-001067
00:56:35.039 --> 00:56:40.240
Rep. Dan S. Fernandez: Si Sec. Solidum, one of the performing secretaries.

asr-001068
00:56:40.240 --> 00:56:41.960
Rep. Dan S. Fernandez: Of course, the entire department, no?

asr-001069
00:56:42.160 --> 00:56:46.880
Rep. Dan S. Fernandez: So, I'm only here to support your budget and if possible, increase your budget.

asr-001070
00:56:46.880 --> 00:56:47.498
Rep. Dan S. Fernandez: Yun lang po.

asr-001071
00:56:51.110 --> 00:56:56.680
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Thank you, SDS. May hahabol lang na question.

asr-001072
00:56:56.680 --> 00:56:58.400
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Congressman Tinio, go ahead.

asr-001073
00:57:01.960 --> 00:57:05.160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Chair, actually, may postscript lang ako doon sa issue ng

asr-001074
00:57:05.799 --> 00:57:09.600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ah, data sovereignty, digital sovereignty, AI sovereignty.

asr-001075
00:57:10.079 --> 00:57:16.020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At may, meron, binanggit nga si Secretary, meron ng national AI strategy.

asr-001076
00:57:16.760 --> 00:57:17.020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay?

asr-001077
00:57:17.680 --> 00:57:20.720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At personally, I support this idea, no?

asr-001078
00:57:20.720 --> 00:57:27.139
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Na, sige, lumalaganap ang AI. Kailangan meron—may control ang mga Pilipino, 'di ba.

asr-001079
00:57:27.280 --> 00:57:29.559
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Hindi yung nakaasa tayo sa AI.

asr-001080
00:57:29.559 --> 00:57:30.900
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: In a way, yung data natin,

asr-001081
00:57:31.280 --> 00:57:37.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: gagamitin nung iba to improve their models and then we, we end up just as paying customers.

asr-001082
00:57:38.319 --> 00:57:39.319
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Hindi tama yun.

asr-001083
00:57:39.319 --> 00:57:44.119
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: However, Mr. Chair, I would like to point something out.

asr-001084
00:57:44.119 --> 00:57:47.560
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Recently, ay kaugnay po ito sa Pax Silica.

asr-001085
00:57:48.400 --> 00:57:56.400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: The main proponent of Pax Silica is the U.S. Undersecretary of State, Jacob Helberg, no?

asr-001086
00:57:56.400 --> 00:58:05.500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And, uh, just last June 24, he came out with a, uh, a, um, um,

asr-001087
00:58:05.599 --> 00:58:10.120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: a speech or a publication called the Digital Sovereignty Trap.

asr-001088
00:58:10.640 --> 00:58:13.080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At dito, explicitly, ang sinasabi niya rito,

asr-001089
00:58:13.680 --> 00:58:19.500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay, a growing number of governments persuaded that independence requires duplication,

asr-001090
00:58:19.839 --> 00:58:26.859
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: are drafting national AI strategies to match, each resolved to rebuild inside its own borders,

asr-001091
00:58:27.240 --> 00:58:30.060
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: a stack that already exists somewhere else.

asr-001092
00:58:30.720 --> 00:58:38.079
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: It is a sub, it is a seductive vision, it is also backward and counterproductive, no?

asr-001093
00:58:38.079 --> 00:58:41.079
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, ang main thesis niya dito, uy, kayong mga bansa,

asr-001094
00:58:41.079 --> 00:58:47.280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: huwag na kayong mag-ambisyong, ah, mag-develop ng sarili niyong AI technology,

asr-001095
00:58:47.880 --> 00:58:49.180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: you will always be backward.

asr-001096
00:58:49.880 --> 00:58:58.960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sumakay kayo sa U.S. kasi we are developing the most advanced AI technology, no?

asr-001097
00:58:58.960 --> 00:59:00.039
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So misguided.

asr-001098
00:59:00.640 --> 00:59:09.880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung, ah, mga plano niyo na magtayo ng sarili niyong, ah, AI technology. Just join us.

asr-001099
00:59:09.880 --> 00:59:14.039
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And this is what Pax Silica is about, no?

asr-001100
00:59:14.039 --> 00:59:18.880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, ah, obviously, tutol po tayo; nire-reject natin.

asr-001101
00:59:19.599 --> 00:59:26.600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung, ayan na 'yun, the main proponent of Pax Silica is this, this person, Helberg.

asr-001102
00:59:27.079 --> 00:59:29.320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Siya nga yung nagpunta rito to inaugurate.

asr-001103
00:59:30.079 --> 00:59:35.559
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: uh, the, the Pax Silica project in, uh, New Clark City, no?

asr-001104
00:59:35.559 --> 00:59:41.480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And napakalinaw po nung kanyang argumento dito na, okay,

asr-001105
00:59:42.400 --> 00:59:46.159
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: huwag na yung digital national, you know, yung no AI sovereignty.

asr-001106
00:59:48.000 --> 00:59:49.420
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Mananatili kayong backward.

asr-001107
00:59:50.559 --> 00:59:55.550
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tulungan niyo kami. Nasa amin ang pinaka-advanced na teknolohiya, no.

asr-001108
00:59:55.640 --> 00:59:56.580
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, um...

asr-001109
00:59:57.960 --> 01:00:04.579
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: In that regard, ah, ano pong masasabi ng DOST diyan?

asr-001110
01:00:05.920 --> 01:00:07.740
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: AI is simply a technology.

asr-001111
01:00:07.920 --> 01:00:09.120
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: It can be powerful.

asr-001112
01:00:09.520 --> 01:00:11.720
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: You can develop large language models.

asr-001113
01:00:12.240 --> 01:00:22.379
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: But in the AI summit that I attended, one of the leading industrial companies,

asr-001114
01:00:23.039 --> 01:00:32.659
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: I think one of the best statements that she made was you cannot compete with those already advanced.

asr-001115
01:00:33.280 --> 01:00:38.920
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: And so her advice is for countries to develop smaller language models

asr-001116
01:00:38.920 --> 01:00:43.619
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: that would address the specific needs of their country or their organization.

asr-001117
01:00:44.119 --> 01:00:48.960
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: Second, it is the data that will be more powerful than the AI.

asr-001118
01:00:49.319 --> 01:00:49.760
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: That is why,

asr-001119
01:00:49.760 --> 01:00:53.560
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: our focus is to develop a data sovereignty platform.

asr-001120
01:00:53.960 --> 01:00:54.680
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: Thank you.

asr-001121
01:00:54.680 --> 01:00:55.839
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-001122
01:00:55.839 --> 01:01:00.920
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: In that regard, uh, I commend the Secretary for having that stand.

asr-001123
01:01:00.920 --> 01:01:07.160
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Importante po, no, na sa kabila ng ayan na po napakalinaw na tulak ng U.S.—

asr-001124
01:01:07.160 --> 01:01:10.040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: sabi nila, tigil niyo na 'yan, sumama kayo sa amin—

asr-001125
01:01:10.720 --> 01:01:18.640
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ah, dapat po, tama lang na ipagpatuloy ang effort na i-develop ang sarili nating infrastructure at

asr-001126
01:01:18.640 --> 01:01:22.119
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: kakayahan kahit dito sa larangan ng AI,

asr-001127
01:01:22.119 --> 01:01:35.620
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: lalo pa at ang kailangan—ang kailangan natin ay 'yung sariling data natin ang gamitin para tugunan ang mga pangangailangan ng Pilipino. Okay. Thank you, Mr. Chair. 'Yun lang po ang puntong gusto kong i-raise. Thank you.

asr-001130
01:01:36.680 --> 01:01:38.870
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Thank you, Congressman Tinio.

