Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So maybe just a few questions, Kong Amben.

asr-001181
01:04:28.680 --> 01:04:29.480
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Very quick.

asr-001182
01:04:29.480 --> 01:04:32.480
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Thank you, Kong Tonshi, for posing a lot of the,

asr-001183
01:04:32.480 --> 01:04:37.720
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: I was going to ask on the agency-wise allocations,

asr-001184
01:04:37.720 --> 01:04:43.179
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: but you explained to Kong Tonshi that the big decreases

asr-001185
01:04:43.200 --> 01:04:46.800
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: in Pag-ASA and PNRI,

asr-001186
01:04:47.240 --> 01:04:50.480
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: it was explained that Pag-ASA is okay

asr-001187
01:04:50.480 --> 01:04:52.140
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: because it's already done.

asr-001188
01:04:53.279 --> 01:04:54.839
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Is that, did I catch it correctly?

asr-001189
01:04:54.839 --> 01:04:57.680
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: The ₱364 million differential is because

asr-001192
01:04:57.680 --> 01:04:59.599
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: uh, on the differential is because there's

asr-001193
01:04:59.599 --> 01:05:03.200
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: a project that was already done already so no need

asr-001194
01:05:03.200 --> 01:05:04.639
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: to fund it for 2027.

asr-001195
01:05:05.520 --> 01:05:07.639
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: For FNRI, it's the building.

asr-001196
01:05:09.960 --> 01:05:12.960
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: For the PNRI, is it the same case po?

asr-001197
01:05:12.960 --> 01:05:16.200
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: It's a project, it's a 345 million decrease.

asr-001198
01:05:17.079 --> 01:05:18.140
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Is it a similar?

asr-001199
01:05:18.520 --> 01:05:19.039
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: Yes.

asr-001200
01:05:19.039 --> 01:05:23.579
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Similar situation po with Pag-ASA or with FNRI?

asr-001201
01:05:24.000 --> 01:05:26.700
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: It's similar with FNRI.

asr-001202
01:05:26.920 --> 01:05:35.480
DOST Secretary Renato U. Solidum Jr.: the project has already done with all its phases kaya nag-stop na po yung funding for this particular capital outlay.

asr-001203
01:05:35.480 --> 01:05:42.200
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Okay. Sige po. So yun na naman po yung malaki. Those are the most glaring reductions.

asr-001204
01:05:42.799 --> 01:05:52.160
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: You also explained to Kongtonchi earlier that the reason for the increases in the different agency budgets is because of the transfer of the grants.

asr-001205
01:05:52.640 --> 01:05:58.880
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So, Sige po, that's where I want to ask a question on, a clarificatory question on.

asr-001206
01:05:58.880 --> 01:06:08.559
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Because earlier it was discussed po that there was a request whether it's possible to re-centralize the grants in the Office of the Secretary.

asr-001207
01:06:08.559 --> 01:06:13.839
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So I just wanted to maybe ask, we also have our DBM family here with us.

asr-001208
01:06:13.839 --> 01:06:22.220
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So, Sek, maybe just to enlighten us as to why the grants were distributed.

asr-001209
01:06:22.240 --> 01:06:28.040
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Across the different agencies. Is that...was that a decision on the part of the OSD or was that the DBM decision?

asr-001210
01:06:30.880 --> 01:06:33.640
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Sorry. Sorry. Sorry, friends, to put you on the spot.

asr-001211
01:06:33.640 --> 01:06:38.119
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: May we request of someone from the DBM family to please enlighten us?

asr-001212
01:06:38.119 --> 01:06:46.000
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Kasi this is, this is a big point of contention. This is 1.25 billion being talked about.

asr-001213
01:06:46.000 --> 01:06:50.059
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So, we just want to understand which way is the right way forward.

asr-001214
01:06:50.520 --> 01:06:54.200
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Do we centralize the grants in the Office of the Secretary

asr-001217
01:06:54.200 --> 01:06:57.039
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: the grants in the Office of the Secretary or do we retain the way that

asr-001218
01:06:57.039 --> 01:07:01.680
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: it's here in the NEP which is distributed across agencies? So if we

asr-001219
01:07:01.680 --> 01:07:18.200
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: could request someone from the DBM. Director Vivian, if you could

asr-001220
01:07:18.200 --> 01:07:23.320
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: introduce yourself Director Vivian to the DOST family and to our colleagues.

asr-001221
